 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Counterexample: `S = (-1)` (1\u00d71, not PSD) gives `CFC.sqrt S = 0` by `CFC.sqrt_of_not_nonneg` (mathlib/.../Rpow/Basic.lean:249), so LHS `det (1 - c \u2022 0) = 1`, while with `\u0398 = 1, c = 1` the RHS is `det (1 + 1) = 2`. The proof at line 68 uses `CFC.sqrt_mul_sqrt_self S hS.nonneg`, which needs PSD.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Matrix/Sqrt.lean",
   "fix": "Add the hypothesis to the prose: \"\u2026whose pencils, *for positive-semidefinite `S`*, have the same determinant as those of `\u0398 * S`\"; likewise qualify the Main-results bullet at line 33.",
   "issue": "Module docstring claims the pencils `1 - c \u2022 (CFC.sqrt S * \u0398 * CFC.sqrt S)` \"have the same determinant as those of `\u0398 * S`\" for an unrestricted `S`; the theorem `PosSemidef.det_one_sub_smul_sqrt_mul_mul_sqrt` (line 65) requires `hS : S.PosSemidef`, and the identity fails without it.",
   "line": 19
  }
 ],
